The discussion focused on a new UNEP report on the economic and health case for integrated climate and clean air action that emphasizes the rapid benefits of such strategies. It highlighted that market benefits, including reduced healthcare costs and increased productivity, outweigh implementation costs within a decade. The report recommends pursuing climate and air quality actions together, predicting significant avoided damages from air pollution and climate change by 2050. Key data from the assessment illustrated that addressing pollution alongside climate change could prevent millions of premature deaths and deliver vast economic gains, reinforcing the importance of integrated strategies.
